<p>In the latest development in the US-Israeli war with Iran, President Trump said the United States would accept no deal other than Iran’s “unconditional surrender.” He also suggested the conflict should be followed by choosing new Iranian leadership acceptable to Washington. His remarks came as fighting moved into a second week, with Israeli strikes continuing in and around Tehran, including reports of explosions at Tehran’s Mehrabad Airport. Separately, some outlets reported intensified Israeli bombardment in Lebanon.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gEUOjCOVlWgw0mlhTrY3qV-incpgcK_H-p1TBtT75ycbAmxkmUW-swTQPh9TP488_9Ic_UPLBldAfw1bGpNtnlHsequ5vrNGAjBWHofzepqajPRkQcpZJjmEGKGWqnbWNmvP1htg4SY7fWqBVYh0MGw7RVyziRmiJzy_eMulC6h7IXxpGaUMuc5TfyVqPg' alt='President Trump declared on Friday that he would settle for nothing short of “unconditional surrender” by Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Postwar pitch: Coverage noted Trump paired the surrender demand with promises of economic rebuilding after the conflict, including rhetoric about making the country “bigger, better, and stronger”.</li><li>Mixed signals: Politico said Trump’s post followed days of mixed messaging from administration officials and described it as leaving Tehran with little off-ramp for negotiations.</li><li>Mediation efforts: Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian said on social media that some countries have begun mediation efforts, while stressing Iran will defend its “dignity”.</li><li>Regional spillover: PBS reported Israel carried out its heaviest strikes in Lebanon since a 2024 ceasefire, after Hezbollah fired rockets early in the current conflict.</li><li>Carrier claim: Iran’s parliament speaker Mohammad-Bagher Ghalibaf said Iranian attacks forced the USS Abraham Lincoln to retreat, according to The Hindu.</li></ul><blockquote>There will be no deal with Iran except UNCONDITIONAL SURRENDER! - Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House (President Trump): Trump said 